<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Menua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Menua was king of Urartu from about 810 to 786 BCE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishpuini">Ishpuini</a>. He enlarged the kingdom by campaigns to the north, west and towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a> and left many inscriptions recording his wars and buildings. His long irrigation canal bringing water to the plain of Van, later attributed to the legendary queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semiramis">Semiramis</a>, is still in use. He was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argishti-i">Argishti I</a>.</p></div>
